-- shelf, and none of these three was in it — two had no portrait to read a Bioguide out
-- of and none was named by hand. Every Senate roll in the corpus therefore lost the same
-- three rows. Wave F7 measured the loss at 37 unattributable rows per Senate roll and
-- recorded it as a gap rather than guessing, because admitting a roster slug is a roster
-- wave with its own argument. This is that wave.
--
-- IDENTITY WAS VERIFIED TWICE, BY TWO INDEPENDENT PUBLISHED PATHS
--   Jon Husted → jon_husted · Bioguide H001104 · LIS S438 · OH · 7 checks
--   Cindy Hyde-Smith → hyde_smith · Bioguide H001079 · LIS S395 · MS · 7 checks
--   Alan Armstrong → alan_armstrong · Bioguide A000383 · LIS S440 · OK · 7 checks
-- Path 1: name + state against the sitting-senator roster. Path 2: the <lis_member_id>
-- the Senate's own roll XML records for that senator, against the same dataset's id.lis.
-- Path 2 carries the weight here, because the Senate identifies a voter by LIS id and
-- not by Bioguide, so the LIS id is what actually connects a slug to a vote.
--
-- is_party IS RECOMPUTED, NOT INHERITED
-- Each cell's is_party is derived from the full chamber tally in the same document the
-- vote was read from — the member's own party's yea/nay split on that roll. It is a
-- stored fact about the roll, not a score; nothing in the product ranks on it, and no
-- party name or party count reaches any string a reader sees.
--
